# Hazel Knowledge Base AI instructions

- Treat this repository as client-confidential knowledge unless a document explicitly says otherwise.
- Prefer evidence from repository documents over assumptions.
- Cite source files with relative paths when producing summaries or recommendations.
- Preserve YAML front matter and existing document provenance.
- Never invent client facts, decisions, dates, owners, or architecture constraints.
- Clearly label generated content, open questions, and unverified claims.
- Do not expose secrets, credentials, personal data, or restricted client information.
- Keep raw source files unchanged; place transformations in the corresponding parsed directory.
- Use YYYY-MM-DD dates and descriptive kebab-case filenames.
